Leo: Really? Why a robot one and not a real puppy?
Mia: Because it doesn''t need to be fed, and it never gets sick.
Leo: That''s true. But can it really respond to you like a real dog?
Mia: The shop says it can learn your voice and obey simple commands.
Leo: Sounds impressive. Still, I think a real dog gives you more love.
Mia: Maybe. A robot can''t build a true emotional bond with you.
Leo: Exactly. I''d rather have a pet that really feels something.', 'Mia 想买那只机器狗,觉得它可爱;Leo 问为何不买真小狗;Mia 说机器狗不用喂、不生病;Leo 问它能否像真狗一样回应;Mia 说它能学声音、听简单命令;Leo 觉得很厉害但真狗更有爱;Mia 承认机器无法建立真正情感联系;Leo 表示更想要有真情感的宠物。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Mia want to buy?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A robot dog.","A real puppy.","A new phone.","A camera."]},{"q":"Why does Mia prefer a robot pet?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It is much cheaper than food.","It needs no feeding and never gets sick.","It can talk like a person.","It can drive a car."]},{"q":"What can the robot dog do, according to the shop?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Learn her voice and obey simple commands.","Cook meals for the family.","Fly around the room.","Repair itself when broken."]},{"q":"What does Leo think a real dog offers?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Less trouble than a robot.","More love than a robot.","A faster Internet link.","Better video games."]},{"q":"What do they finally agree on?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Robots are always better than real pets.","Real dogs are too expensive.","A robot can''t build a true emotional bond.","Nobody should keep any pet."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U4', 'sufe');
Most of all, they are afraid that new machines will make them lose their jobs.
Some say that robots may increase the gap between the rich and the poor.
Many would not ride in a self-driving car without a human in the seat.
Yet the report also notes that technology, used wisely, can save lives and time.', '一份最新报告显示许多人担忧新科技;他们最害怕新机器让自己失业;有人说机器人可能拉大贫富差距;许多人不愿乘坐没有人在驾驶座的自动驾驶车;但报告也指出,明智地使用科技能挽救生命、节省时间。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What are people most afraid of, according to the report?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Running out of phones.","Having no Internet at all.","Driving too slowly.","Losing their jobs to machines."]},{"q":"What might robots increase, some people say?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The gap between rich and poor.","The price of food.","The number of real dogs.","The speed of trains."]},{"q":"What would many people not do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Use a smartphone at all.","Ride in a self-driving car with no human in the seat.","Visit a hospital.","Watch the news."]},{"q":"What does the report also note about technology?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It always destroys jobs.","It is useless in hospitals.","Used wisely, it can save lives and time.","It can never be trusted."]},{"q":"What is the main idea of the report?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["All new technology should be banned.","Robots already control the world.","Self-driving cars are perfectly safe.","People worry about technology but it can also help."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U4', 'sufe');
Sam: From another city? How is that even possible?
Nina: He used a 5G connection to direct the local team in real time.
Sam: So the specialist didn''t have to travel to the patient at all?
Nina: Right. He just needed a fast and stable Internet link.
Sam: But what if the signal had a delay? That sounds risky.
Nina: With 5G the delay is only about one millisecond, so it''s safe.
Sam: Amazing. That could really help patients in remote places.', 'Nina 说一位医生从另一座城市做了心脏手术;Sam 惊讶问怎么可能;Nina 说他用5G实时指挥当地团队;Sam 问专家因此完全不用奔波;Nina 说对,只需快速稳定的网络;Sam 担心信号延迟有风险;Nina 说5G延迟仅约一毫秒,很安全;Sam 感叹这能真正帮到偏远地区的病人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where was the doctor during the operation?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["In another city, far from the patient.","In the same room as the patient.","On a plane to the hospital.","At the patient''s home."]},{"q":"What did the doctor use to direct the team?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A paper letter.","A 5G connection in real time.","A loud telephone.","A printed map."]},{"q":"What did the specialist need most?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A faster car.","A bigger operating room.","A fast and stable Internet link.","More nurses on the plane."]},{"q":"Why is 5G safe enough for this, Nina says?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It never uses electricity.","It is slower than 4G.","It needs no signal at all.","Its delay is only about one millisecond."]},{"q":"Who could this technology especially help?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Patients in remote places.","Drivers in big cities.","Students learning music.","Cooks in restaurants."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U4', 'sufe');
Its biggest advantage is that it greatly reduces signal delay.
With 4G, the delay can be between twenty and eighty milliseconds.
With 5G, the delay drops to about one millisecond.
This small change makes a huge difference when a robot is controlled from far away.', '5G网络比我们目前使用的4G快很多倍;它最大的优势是大幅减少信号延迟;用4G延迟在20到80毫秒之间;用5G延迟降到约一毫秒;这个微小变化在远程控制机器人时会带来巨大差别。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How does 5G compare with 4G?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It is much slower.","It is many times faster.","It is exactly the same.","It uses no signal."]},{"q":"What is 5G''s biggest advantage?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It makes phones cheaper.","It removes all cameras.","It greatly reduces signal delay.","It stops the Internet."]},{"q":"What is the delay with 4G?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Exactly one millisecond.","A full minute.","No delay at all.","Between twenty and eighty milliseconds."]},{"q":"What is the delay with 5G?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["About one millisecond.","About eighty milliseconds.","About one minute.","About one hour."]},{"q":"When does this small change matter most?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["When you watch a film at home.","When a robot is controlled from far away.","When you read a paper book.","When you walk to school."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U4', 'sufe');
Ella: Sure. You just connect it to the Internet and give it a name.
Dad: And then it really responds when I speak to it?
Ella: Yes. Say "turn on the lights" and watch what happens.
Dad: Wow, the room lit up at once! That''s quite impressive.
Ella: You can also use your phone to view the front door from anywhere.
Dad: That''s handy. But what happens if the Internet goes down?
Ella: Then nothing smart works, so we still keep the normal switches.', '爸爸说这个新音箱能控制所有灯,让 Ella 帮忙设置;Ella 说连网并取名即可;爸爸问它真能在他说话时回应吗;Ella 让他说“开灯”看看;爸爸惊喜灯立刻亮了,觉得很厉害;Ella 说还能用手机随处查看前门;爸爸问断网怎么办;Ella 说那时智能功能都失灵,所以仍保留普通开关。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the new speaker supposed to control?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The family car.","The kitchen oven only.","All the lights in the home.","The front garden."]},{"q":"How do you set up the speaker, Ella says?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Take it apart and clean it.","Plug it into the television.","Charge it for a whole day.","Connect it to the Internet and give it a name."]},{"q":"What does Dad think after the lights come on?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It is quite impressive.","It is rather boring.","It is too slow.","It is broken."]},{"q":"What else can the phone do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Cook dinner by itself.","View the front door from anywhere.","Drive the car home.","Charge the speaker."]},{"q":"Why do they keep the normal switches?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Because the speaker is too loud.","Because the lights are too bright.","Because nothing smart works if the Internet goes down.","Because Ella dislikes phones."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U4', 'sufe');
When you type a message, it guesses the next word you want.
When you open a music app, it recommends songs you may enjoy.
In hospitals, it can study medical images and help doctors find problems.
But AI has no real feelings, so people and machines work best together.', '人工智能已悄然融入我们的日常生活;打字时它会猜你想用的下一个词;打开音乐App时它推荐你可能喜欢的歌;在医院它能研究医学影像、帮医生发现问题;但AI没有真正的情感,所以人与机器合作效果最好。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does AI do when you type a message?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It deletes the message.","It calls your friend.","It turns off the phone.","It guesses the next word you want."]},{"q":"What does AI do in a music app?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Recommends songs you may enjoy.","Stops all the music.","Records your voice.","Charges the battery."]},{"q":"How does AI help in hospitals?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It builds the hospital walls.","It studies medical images to help find problems.","It feeds the patients.","It drives the ambulance."]},{"q":"What does AI lack, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Electric power.","Any useful skill.","Real feelings.","A connection to the Internet."]},{"q":"What works best, the speaker says?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Machines working completely alone.","Banning AI from daily life.","Letting AI make every choice.","People and machines working together."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U4', 'sufe');

